<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yu'fir ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hiwali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yu'fir ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hiwali was a Yemeni chief of the Himyarite Hiwal tribe who founded the Yufirid dynasty in the 9th century. Around 847 he seized the highland fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shibam-kawkaban">Shibam Kawkaban</a> and soon took Sanaa from the Abbasid governors, ruling much of the Yemeni highlands while still acknowledging the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khutba">Friday prayer</a>.</p></div>
